fix: CLI TLS + mTLS + agent command splitting for full e2e flow

Four fixes to make `trybox "hello world"` work end-to-end:

1. SHA256 cert signing: LibreSSL defaults to SHA1 for x509 -req,
   which rustls rejects. Added -sha256 to server/client cert signing.

2. mTLS cert provisioning: `openshell gateway add --local` requires
   client certs in ~/.config/openshell/gateways/<name>/mtls/ BEFORE
   the add command runs. Copy CA + client cert + key there first.

3. Gateway re-registration: handle "already exists" gracefully by
   falling back to `gateway select` instead of failing.

4. Agent command splitting: `--agent "sleep 3600"` was passed as a
   single argument. Use shlex.split() to properly split into
   ["sleep", "3600"] for the openshell sandbox create -- args.

E2E verified: trybox "hello world" → create (Ready) → exec → stop →
start (resume, Ready) → exec after resume. Full 5/5 lifecycle.
